      "rationale": "L1 explicitly states the Myc tag was inserted into ECL2 of full-length AQP5 'after amino acid N117'; the amino acid letter N identifies asparagine, which in the canonical UniProt sequence sits at position 116 (not 117, which is L). Python search confirms N116 is the only asparagine at that position in ECL2, so the paper's numbering is offset by +1 relative to canonical. The junction is therefore insert_after_residue=116 (residue_before=N, residue_after=L), confirmed extracellular and \u22653 residues from both flanking TM helices. L2 independently confirms plasma membrane surface display of this exact construct. Full-length AQP5 with Myc tag flanked by alanines inserted into ECL2 after the paper's 'N117' (asparagine), expressed as AQP5-myc-EGFP in stably transfected MDCK cells. The paper's residue label 'N117' names an asparagine; canonical position 117 = L (leucine), canonical position 116 = N (asparagine), indicating a 1-residue offset in the paper's numbering. The tag was placed after canonical N116, which lies 8 residues from the TM3 boundary (ends at 108) and 16 residues from the TM4 boundary (starts at 132), well within ECL2 (109\u2013131).",
